      "reason": "A person's body: the VRM 1.0 humanoid's 55 bone names and parents, 15 of them required, so a look of any origin that maps its joints onto them (a rigged mesh, rigid blocky parts, a game's character) moves and holds things on the same named bones. Rest pose T-pose; in the world's slot frame up is +z and the front +y, which a glTF look (+Y up, +Z front) meets by the style packs' rotation. Two hand sockets each hold one thing at most 1,500 mm long (a sword of 1,000 mm, never a 1,800 mm bench) whose section through its grip is at most 60 mm (a closed adult hand around a hilt or a handle: a declared figure, not a measurement). Heights from 900 to 2,400 mm cover a child-sized figure to a tall armoured one; the walking module's clearance and the society's object reach of 1,500 mm hold for every height, so a body's height changes how it is drawn, never where it may go. Idle and walk are required of every look; run, reach, hold, talk and sit are drawn where a look has them and otherwise stood idle, never replaced by a pose that implies another action.",
